<title>FRANCE: CYCLING-CIPOLLINI WITHDRAWS FROM TOUR DE FRANCE.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-CIPOLLINI WITHDRAWS FROM TOUR DE FRANCE.</headline>
<dateline>MARENNES, France 1997-07-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian sprinter Mario Cipollini withdrew from the 194-km seventh stage of the Tour de France cycle race on Saturday.</p>
<p>Cipollini, who won the first two stages and wore the yellow jersey for four days, stopped after 25 kms because of a knee injury sustained in a mass fall on Friday.</p>
